        "original_id": "129b3f24-58e0-5df6-a820-2cd9edde1a29",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Portland International Airport, Gerald R. Ford International Airport, Oregon, Cascade Township, Grand Rapids, Michigan, California\n- Organizations: 454th Bombardment Group, 454th Troop Carrier Wing, Continental Air Command\n- Concepts: airport codes, civil-military airports, commercial airports, air cargo, passenger travel, native habitat\n\nFacts:\n- Portland International Airport has the airport codes IATA PDX, ICAO KPDX, and FAA LID PDX.\n- Portland International Airport is a joint civil-military airport and the largest airport in Oregon.\n- Portland International Airport accounts for 90 percent of Oregon's passenger travel and more than 95 percent of the state's air cargo.\n- The 454th Bombardment Group was last assigned to the 454th Troop Carrier Wing of Continental Air Command at Portland International Airport in Oregon.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport has the airport codes IATA GRR, ICAO KGRR, and FAA LID GRR.\n- Gerald R. Ford International Airport is a commercial airport in Cascade Township about 13 miles southeast of Grand Rapids, Michigan.\n- Carex barbarae is native to California and Oregon.\n- Carex barbarae grows in wet and seasonally wet habitats such as meadows and riverbanks.",
